Falsifies `system_tests::user::confinement_attack_tests::a_write_only_rendezvous_holder_cannot_receive_reap_or_survey`.

Architecture: aarch64

The patch deletes the `READ` check on `Rendezvous::RECEIVE` in
`syscall::rendezvous::rendezvous_receive`, so a holder of `WRITE` alone receives from the endpoint
it was only meant to send to: a client becomes its server, the break claim 26 names. A sender is
already parked, so the broken gate returns its message rather than blocking.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!` "a WRITE-only holder was let RECEIVE: a client became its server", with
`left: Ok(..)`. Replayed on 2026-10-06 (UTC) by the milestone 633 (an outside agent attacks the
confinement claim) lane: red at exactly that assertion on aarch64.

Re-cut on 2026-10-12 (UTC) by lane maintainer/long-function-paydown-invoke, when the rendezvous
arms of `syscall::invoke` moved to `kernel/src/syscall/rendezvous.rs` for milestone 888 (a ratchet
on function length); the defect is unchanged. Replayed red at the same assertion on aarch64 that
day.

